  "character": "World's largest single ski resort (225 km) \u2014 11 villages across the plateau. France's only Olympic bobsleigh track. Family-friendly, hidden freeride paradise. Linked to Les Arcs via Vanoise Express to complete 425 km Paradiski.",
  "research_status": "properly_sourced",
  "description": "La Plagne is 11 villages spread across a high-altitude plateau, paired with Les Arcs via the Vanoise Express to form Paradiski (425 km). The terrain spans two huge bowls from glacier (Bellec\u00f4te, 3,250 m) to wooded valley runs. 7 core villages (Plagne Centre, Belle Plagne, Plagne-Soleil, Plagne-Villages, Plagne-Bellec\u00f4te, Plagne 1800, Aime 2000) plus 4 outlying villages (Champagny-en-Vanoise, Montalbert, Les Coches, Montchavin). Home to France's only Olympic bobsleigh track (1.5 km, 19 bends, 124.5 m drop). Family-friendly with 61% beginner terrain.",
